.TH LIONCTL-LOCKER 1 "2026" "LionOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lionctl-locker \- control the LionOS screen locker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lionctl locker
.RI [ status | lock | unlock | signals | reload | check | version | schema ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Thin wrapper around
.BR busctl (1)
for the
.B os.lionos.Locker1
service.
.TP
.B status
Print IsLocked, State and Failures.
.TP
.B lock
Lock the screen now.
.TP
.B unlock
Call Unlock(). Succeeds only right after a local PAM authentication in
explicit-unlock mode; otherwise the daemon denies it by design.
.TP
.B signals
Monitor Locked, Unlocked and AuthFailed.
.TP
.B reload
Ask systemd to send SIGHUP to the daemon.
.TP
.B check
Validate the configuration file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LION_LOCKER_CONFIG
Configuration path (default /etc/lion/locker.json).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lion-locker (8)
